"author": "elemental.math", "author_id": "22981797247", "id": "18130479409829213", "text": "Every Reel on this account is made by an AI agent I built (yes, this one too).\n\nComment AGENT and I\u2019ll DM you a version for your own account \ud83d\udce9 \n\nOr open getopenreels.com from the link in my bio.", "timestamp": 1793024693, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "narsus9", "author_id": "1706552537", "id": "17922534423452175", "text": "Maxxing gooning", "timestamp": 1792863251, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "octo.pod", "author_id": "6308079829", "id": "18079578932386897", "text": "Be very careful with these mazes in videogames, especially with the simplest ones as they are spanning trees and it's extremely un-fun to walk through them yourselves. It's OK, if you see it from the top, but if you are inside it's awful.", "timestamp": 1792611280, "like_count": 1}, {"author": "yyc_tom", "author_id": "201749704", "id": "18182245126437025", "text": "Oh\u2026 I like this.\n.\nImagine generating and then navigating a maze in a higher dimension. 3rd\u2026 easy. 4th\u2026 umm\u2026 5th dimension? Whadda ya do? Keep using the left hand rule??", "timestamp": 1792103507, "like_count": 1}, {"author": "jose.breijo", "author_id": "2108877094", "id": "18131308450667714", "text": "Implementing wave function collapse is a nice exercise to practice drawing.", "timestamp": 1792026312, "like_count": 4}, {"author": "sevannajarian", "author_id": "33379921", "id": "17993523093028375", "text": "i use this for almost every initial design.", "timestamp": 1791992992, "like_count": 2}, {"author": "sciloj", "author_id": "1798909720", "id": "18110410832612755", "text": "Very similar to the Lindenmayer system.", "timestamp": 1791958590, "like_count": 2}, {"author": "senku9083", "author_id": "52011558029", "id": "18168123871415095", "text": "Sounds like conway's game of life", "timestamp": 1791943672, "like_count": 3}, {"author": "arch1tector", "author_id": "490299985", "id": "18030847721683679", "text": 